  "worked_solution": "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-{450}^{\u2218}$ by *adding* integer multiples of ${360}^{\u2218}$ until we get an angle that lies in the range $[{0}^{\u2218},{360}^{\u2218}).$\n\n- $-{450}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}=-90$\n\n- $-{450}^{\u2218}+2\\cdot {360}^{\u2218}={270}^{\u2218}\\,\u2713$\n\nSo the angle ${270}^{\u2218}$ is coterminal with $-{450}^{\u2218}.$ Let's draw this coterminal angle in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13939908/assets/35b9783c9ac87b0a8d177e7bdf340b48513146404b7c768a8532da59b6ec7948.png)\n\nWe see that ${270}^{\u2218}$ lies between quadrants III and IV. Therefore, $-{450}^{\u2218}$ also lies between these quadrants.",
